00:52:38,660 --> 00:52:40,162
I DON'T WEAR MAKEUP,

1650
00:52:40,162 --> 00:52:41,797
SO I DON'T REALLY KNOW
WHAT TO DO.

1651
00:52:41,797 --> 00:52:42,831
WHEN YOU DON'T
KNOW WHAT YOU'RE DOING,

1652
00:52:42,831 --> 00:52:44,399
YOU BETTER STICK TO
WHAT YOU KNOW.

1653
00:52:44,399 --> 00:52:45,667
PUT ON A
LITTLE MASCARA,

1654
00:52:45,667 --> 00:52:47,402
LITTLE GLOSS AND
POOF UP THE HAIR.

1655
00:52:51,740 --> 00:52:52,341
WHAT?

1656
00:52:52,341 --> 00:52:54,042
I'VE NEVER PUT ON MAKEUP
BEFORE EVER.

1657
00:52:54,042 --> 00:52:55,043
DUDE.

1658
00:52:55,043 --> 00:52:56,578
KIM IS FREAKING
OUT RIGHT NOW

1659
00:52:56,578 --> 00:52:58,347
BECAUSE SHE DOES NOT
WEAR MAKEUP.

1660
00:52:58,347 --> 00:53:00,716
I DON'T
KNOW WHAT TO DO.

1661
00:53:00,716 --> 00:53:02,651
THIS IS--I WANNA WRITE
WITH THIS.

1662
00:53:02,651 --> 00:53:03,552
HEY, WHO
WANTS TO HELP ME

1663
00:53:03,552 --> 00:53:04,319
WITH MY EYE LINER?

1664
00:53:04,319 --> 00:53:05,587
'CAUSE I DON'T KNOW
HOW TO PUT IT ON.

1665
00:53:05,587 --> 00:53:07,890
♪♪♪

1666
00:53:07,890 --> 00:53:09,725
OBVIOUSLY, WE HAVE
TO DO OUR OWN MAKEUP,

1667
00:53:09,725 --> 00:53:11,093
AND KIM GOES TO ASHLEY,

1668
00:53:11,093 --> 00:53:13,095
SHE'S LIKE, "I NEED HELP
WITH MY MAKEUP,"

1669
00:53:13,095 --> 00:53:14,663
AND ASHLEY WAS LIKE,

1670
00:53:14,663 --> 00:53:17,232
"WELL, YOU BETTER
FIGURE IT OUT."

1671
00:53:17,232 --> 00:53:19,434
AND KIM WAS LIKE,
"AREN'T WE ROOMMATES?

1672
00:53:19,434 --> 00:53:21,069
LIKE, AREN'T YOU SUPPOSED
TO HELP ME?"

1673
00:53:21,069 --> 00:53:23,972
I WAS LIKE,
"THAT IS SO RUDE."

1674
00:53:23,972 --> 00:53:24,973
HERE, I'LL HELP YOU.

1675
00:53:24,973 --> 00:53:26,708
I LITERALLY HAVE
NO IDEA HOW TO DO THIS.

1676
00:53:26,708 --> 00:53:27,709
OKAY.

1677
00:53:27,709 --> 00:53:28,710
I KNOW THAT
THERE WERE GIRLS

1678
00:53:28,710 --> 00:53:29,811
WHO WERE HELPING
PEOPLE OUT,

1679
00:53:29,811 --> 00:53:31,346
BUT I WASN'T
HELPING ANYBODY.

1680
00:53:31,346 --> 00:53:32,648
THAT WASN'T MY
CONCERN

1681
00:53:32,648 --> 00:53:34,983
BECAUSE THIS
IS A COMPETITION.

1682
00:53:34,983 --> 00:53:36,785
YEAH, I DEFINITELY
WONDER WHY,

1683
00:53:36,785 --> 00:53:37,819
SINCE WE'RE SUCH
GOOD FRIENDS,

1684
00:53:37,819 --> 00:53:38,887
SHE CAN'T
HELP ME OUT.

1685
00:53:38,887 --> 00:53:40,722
ALSO, YOU KNOW,
IT MAKES ME REALIZE THAT

1686
00:53:40,722 --> 00:53:42,157
AS MUCH AS I
LIKE ASHLEY,

1687
00:53:42,157 --> 00:53:43,959
SHE'S NOT SOMEONE THAT
I CAN TRUST.

1688
00:53:43,959 --> 00:53:46,762
♪♪♪

1689
00:53:50,365 --> 00:53:53,001
THE RUNWAY.

1690
00:53:53,001 --> 00:53:55,737
IT IS THE MOST
HECTIC PUZZLE EVER.

1691
00:53:55,737 --> 00:53:58,073
♪♪♪

1692
00:53:58,073 --> 00:54:00,242
I THINK THEY'D GIVE US
THIS CRAZY RUNWAY--

1693
00:54:00,242 --> 00:54:02,311
THE SQUARE SHAPE--
FOR A REASON.

1694
00:54:02,311 --> 00:54:04,479
AND SO THERE'S GONNA
BE TWO DIFFERENT PEOPLE

1695
00:54:04,479 --> 00:54:06,315
GOING ON THE STAGE
AT ONE TIME.

1696
00:54:06,315 --> 00:54:08,083
SOME OF US
WILL HAVE TO GO ONE WAY

1697
00:54:08,083 --> 00:54:09,518
AND THE OTHER GIRLS HAVE
TO GO ANOTHER WAY.

1698
00:54:09,518 --> 00:54:10,919
BUT EVENTUALLY WE CROSS.

1699
00:54:10,919 --> 00:54:14,790
AND WE'RE PROBABLY GONNA
SLIDE AND FALL ON OUR FACE.

1700
00:54:14,790 --> 00:54:16,892
THERE ARE SO MANY
PEOPLE BACKSTAGE,

1701
00:54:16,892 --> 00:54:18,593
AND WE'RE JUST LOOKING
FOR A PLACE

1702
00:54:18,593 --> 00:54:21,830
WHERE WE CAN PRACTICE
OUR WALK IN THESE SHOES.

1703
00:54:21,830 --> 00:54:23,198
I THINK I HAVE THE
WORST WALK.

1704
00:54:23,198 --> 00:54:26,735
♪♪♪

1705
00:54:26,735 --> 00:54:27,769
YOU A
LITTLE SHAKY THERE,

1706
00:54:27,769 --> 00:54:28,770
- AREN'T YOU?
- I DON'T LIKE TO WALK,

1707
00:54:28,770 --> 00:54:30,072
AND MY FEET
WEREN'T SWEATING.

1708
00:54:30,072 --> 00:54:32,240
ACTUALLY, I DON'T REALLY
THINK I HAVE A BAD WALK,

1709
00:54:32,240 --> 00:54:34,843
I THINK I JUST HAVE
BAD BALANCE.

1710
00:54:34,843 --> 00:54:37,512
WELCOME TO THE REAL,
GLAMOROUS LIFE OF MODELS.

1711
00:54:37,512 --> 00:54:38,847
I'M GONNA INTRODUCE
YOU GIRLS

1712
00:54:38,847 --> 00:54:40,682
REALLY QUICKLY
TO NATE DOGG,

1713
00:54:40,682 --> 00:54:42,584
WHO IS GONNA BE AN M.C.
HERE TONIGHT.

1714
00:54:42,584 --> 00:54:43,552
(cheering)

1715
00:54:43,552 --> 00:54:44,286
GOOD TO
SEE YOU AGAIN.

1716
00:54:44,286 --> 00:54:45,420
HEY, WHAT'S UP, MAN,
HOW ARE YOU?

1717
00:54:45,420 --> 00:54:46,555
SO, THESE ARE
OUR GIRLS.

1718
00:54:46,555 --> 00:54:47,289
THEY LOOK
GREAT, DON'T THEY?

1719
00:54:47,289 --> 00:54:48,290
WHAT'S UP, LADIES?

1720
00:54:48,290 --> 00:54:51,994
NATE DOGG IS A
HIP-HOP ICON.

1721
00:54:51,994 --> 00:54:53,061
HE'S GREAT.

1722
00:54:53,061 --> 00:54:54,796
HE'S GONNA BE
GIVING YOU THE VIBE

1723
00:54:54,796 --> 00:54:55,931
FOR YOUR WALK.

1724
00:54:55,931 --> 00:54:59,634
AND IT IS SO IMPORTANT TO
KINDA TAKE ON WHAT HE SAYS

1725
00:54:59,634 --> 00:55:01,470
AND THEN PUT YOUR
TOP MODEL SPIN ON IT.

1726
00:55:01,470 --> 00:55:02,537
- ALL RIGHT?
- THAT THEY ARE.

1727
00:55:02,537 --> 00:55:03,638
SO YOU'RE GONNA SEE
THEM OUT THERE,

1728
00:55:03,638 --> 00:55:04,873
AND WE'RE GETTING
READY TO START THE SHOW?

1729
00:55:04,873 --> 00:55:05,907
- LET'S DO IT.
- ALL RIGHT.

1730
00:55:05,907 --> 00:55:08,677
(screaming)

1731
00:55:08,677 --> 00:55:10,145
♪♪♪

1732
00:55:10,145 --> 00:55:11,646
OKAY, ASHLEY, GO.

1733
00:55:11,646 --> 00:55:13,882
THE GRACE
OF A SENSUAL WOMAN.

1734
00:55:13,882 --> 00:55:16,151
♪♪♪

1735
00:55:16,151 --> 00:55:17,786
'CAUSE I WAS THE FIRST
ONE OUT.

1736
00:55:17,786 --> 00:55:19,855
THAT WAS A REALLY
GOOD BOOST OF ENERGY.

1737
00:55:19,855 --> 00:55:22,824
QUIRKY GIRLS ARE
COLORFUL.

1738
00:55:22,824 --> 00:55:24,726
OH, NO, I WAS
FIERCE ON THAT RUNWAY.

1739
00:55:24,726 --> 00:55:25,560
I WAS FIERCE.

1740
00:55:25,560 --> 00:55:27,562
THE POSH LADY.

1741
00:55:27,562 --> 00:55:28,797
I FEEL GREAT ON
THE RUNWAY.

1742
00:55:28,797 --> 00:55:30,065
I'M WALKING DOWN
AND I'M THINKING,

1743
00:55:30,065 --> 00:55:31,633
THIS IS A LOT OF FUN.

1744
00:55:31,633 --> 00:55:32,667
THIS IS NO PROBLEM.

1745
00:55:32,667 --> 00:55:33,468
I CAN DO THIS.

1746
00:55:33,468 --> 00:55:36,338
♪♪♪

1747
00:55:36,338 --> 00:55:37,773
WHAT'S MAKING
THIS CHALLENGE HARD

1748
00:55:37,773 --> 00:55:39,875
IS THE GIRLS WERE
MESSING UP,

1749
00:55:39,875 --> 00:55:41,143
GOING THE WRONG WAY.

1750
00:55:41,143 --> 00:55:42,978
SO THERE'S DEFINITELY
GONNA BE SOME COLLISIONS,

1751
00:55:42,978 --> 00:55:44,212
I'M FEELING.

1752
00:55:46,815 --> 00:55:48,383
LET'S HOPE
I'M NOT ONE OF THEM.

1753
00:55:50,519 --> 00:55:52,888
HOW DOES A SPUNKY
GIRL WALK?

1754
00:55:52,888 --> 00:55:56,725
♪♪♪

1755
00:55:56,725 --> 00:56:00,328
CUTTING-EDGE TRENDSETTER
CAN RULE ANY GOWN.

1756
00:56:01,363 --> 00:56:02,497
I LIKE THE RUNWAY.

1757
00:56:02,497 --> 00:56:04,332
I HAVEN'T EVER SEEN
MYSELF WALK A RUNWAY

1758
00:56:04,332 --> 00:56:06,134
AND I'M PROBABLY
GONNA LAUGH WHEN I DO.

1759
00:56:06,134 --> 00:56:08,503
BUT I LOVE HAVING PEOPLE,
LIKE, WATCH ME.

1760
00:56:08,503 --> 00:56:11,807
♪♪♪

1761
00:56:18,613 --> 00:56:20,749
WHEN IT'S MY TURN,
I LOOK LIKE A CHICKEN

1762
00:56:20,749 --> 00:56:22,050
WITH MY HEAD CUT
OFF, I THINK.

1763
00:56:22,050 --> 00:56:25,353
DANGEROUS.

1764
00:56:25,353 --> 00:56:27,622
SO I WALK OUT THERE
AND, LIKE, I KNEW

1765
00:56:27,622 --> 00:56:29,224
I WAS GONNA FALL.

1766
00:56:29,224 --> 00:56:31,426
IT'S NOT A FULL-OUT FALL,
THANK GOD.

1767
00:56:31,426 --> 00:56:33,228
BUT IT WAS
HUMILIATING.

1768
00:56:33,228 --> 00:56:34,362
AND SHE'S STILL FINE.

1769
00:56:34,362 --> 00:56:36,698
MMM, MMM, MMM.

1770
00:56:36,698 --> 00:56:39,234
ASHLEY, YOU'RE UP.

1771
00:56:39,234 --> 00:56:42,204
♪♪♪

1772
00:56:45,040 --> 00:56:46,341
ALL THE STRESS
BACKSTAGE

1773
00:56:46,341 --> 00:56:48,076
AT THE RUNWAY
SHOW, IT'S CRAZY.

1774
00:56:48,076 --> 00:56:49,077
HURRY, GIRLS.

1775
00:56:49,077 --> 00:56:50,378
WORK IT OUT.

1776
00:56:50,378 --> 00:56:51,947
COME ON,
I NEED SOMEBODY NOW.

1777
00:56:51,947 --> 00:56:53,014
I LOVE THE CHAOS.

1778
00:56:53,014 --> 00:56:54,149
I'M, LIKE, "I'M
IN THE MIDDLE OF CHAOS,

1779
00:56:54,149 --> 00:56:54,916
THIS IS COOL."

1780
00:56:54,916 --> 00:56:56,218
SARAH, COME ON,
GET OUT THERE.

1781
00:56:56,218 --> 00:56:57,752
SARAH HAS
THE WORST WALK.

1782
00:56:57,752 --> 00:56:59,254
SHE NEEDS SOME WALKING
LESSONS

1783
00:56:59,254 --> 00:57:00,255
REAL QUICK HERE.

1784
00:57:00,255 --> 00:57:03,024
THIS ONE IS STILL
QUITE QUEENLY.

1785
00:57:05,760 --> 00:57:07,395
AND THEN I DID
THE SAME THING AGAIN.

1786
00:57:09,731 --> 00:57:11,133
OHH!

1787
00:57:12,801 --> 00:57:15,537
THE TRIPPING DOESN'T
REALLY MAKE ME FEEL GREAT.

1788
00:57:15,537 --> 00:57:17,572
I JUST HUMILIATED
MYSELF TWICE.

1789
00:57:17,572 --> 00:57:21,176
♪♪♪

1790
00:57:21,176 --> 00:57:22,344
HEY, I WANT
TO THANK YOU GUYS

1791
00:57:22,344 --> 00:57:24,646
FOR COMING OUT AND HAVE
A GREAT NIGHT.

1792
00:57:24,646 --> 00:57:25,647
THAT'S IT, RIGHT?

1793
00:57:25,647 --> 00:57:26,781
THAT'S IT, THAT'S IT.

1794
00:57:26,781 --> 00:57:28,917
I THINK IT CAME OUT
GOOD, BUT I THINK PEOPLE

1795
00:57:28,917 --> 00:57:33,121
PROBABLY NOTICED THAT WE
WERE AMATEUR MODELS.

1796
00:57:33,121 --> 00:57:35,323
ALL RIGHT, SO I'M
GONNA SEE YOU GUYS LATER.

1797
00:57:35,323 --> 00:57:37,392
I HONESTLY HAVE TO SAY
THAT WAS THE ABSOLUTELY

1798
00:57:37,392 --> 00:57:39,528
WORST FASHION
SHOW I'VE EVER DONE

1799
00:57:39,528 --> 00:57:41,129
'CAUSE HALF OF YOU WENT
THE WRONG WAY.

1800
00:57:41,129 --> 00:57:42,030
GOOD TRY, THOUGH.

1801
00:57:42,030 --> 00:57:43,498
(cheering)

1802
00:57:43,498 --> 00:57:44,533
I'M GONNA
SEE YOU GUYS SOON.

1803
00:57:44,533 --> 00:57:47,135
(cheering)

1804
00:57:47,135 --> 00:57:49,905
♪♪♪

1805
00:57:49,905 --> 00:57:51,840
OH, MY GOD.

1806
00:57:51,840 --> 00:57:53,208
BRITTNEY'S NAKED!

1807
00:57:53,208 --> 00:57:54,576
(squealing)

1808
00:57:54,576 --> 00:57:57,779
WHEN WE GOT INTO THE LIMO,
A LOT OF GIRLS GOT LOOSE.

1809
00:57:57,779 --> 00:57:59,848
WE LEFT FROM THE PARTY,
THEY STILL WANTED

1810
00:57:59,848 --> 00:58:01,349
TO TAKE
THE PARTY WITH US.

1811
00:58:01,349 --> 00:58:02,350
HEY, WHAT'S UP,
BEAUTIFUL GIRL?

1812
00:58:02,350 --> 00:58:03,618
WHAT'S WRONG WITH YOU?

1813
00:58:03,618 --> 00:58:05,287
KIM, YOU THINK I'M
BEAUTIFUL?

1814
00:58:05,287 --> 00:58:07,189
YEAH.

1815
00:58:07,189 --> 00:58:08,757
(squealing)

1816
00:58:08,757 --> 00:58:10,091
ALL OF THE SUDDEN
JUST SARAH IS

1817
00:58:10,091 --> 00:58:11,126
JUMPING OVER THE SEAT

1818
00:58:11,126 --> 00:58:12,694
AND STARTS MAKING OUT
WITH KIM.

1819
00:58:12,694 --> 00:58:14,296
YEAH!

1820
00:58:14,296 --> 00:58:16,398
I DIDN'T REALLY THINK THAT
THAT WAS GONNA HAPPEN.

1821
00:58:16,398 --> 00:58:17,933
(laughing)

1822
00:58:17,933 --> 00:58:19,401
OH, MY GOD.

1823
00:58:19,401 --> 00:58:22,070
HER TONGUE'S
STICKING OUT.

1824
00:58:22,070 --> 00:58:24,406
AND SHE'S GOT SOME CRAZY
CANTALOUPE LIPS.

1825
00:58:27,676 --> 00:58:29,077
QUIET, QUIET, QUIET.

1826
00:58:29,077 --> 00:58:31,179
ONE DOWN, 11 TO GO.

1827
00:58:31,179 --> 00:58:32,647
♪♪♪

1828
00:58:36,818 --> 00:58:37,419
♪♪♪

1829
00:58:37,419 --> 00:58:39,221
YEAH, THIS IS BROADENING
MY HORIZONS.

1830
00:58:39,221 --> 00:58:40,989
LIKE, KIM
IS LIKE THIS GREAT--

1831
00:58:40,989 --> 00:58:42,557
LIKE, DUDE, SHE'S, LIKE,
A LESBIAN.

1832
00:58:42,557 --> 00:58:44,626
SHE'S GOT
ALL THESE DYNAMICS.

1833
00:58:44,626 --> 00:58:47,062
EVERYONE IS LIKE
EIGHT LAYERS DEEP.

1834
00:58:47,062 --> 00:58:48,363
THERE IS ONLY ONE PERSON

1835
00:58:48,363 --> 00:58:50,899
THAT I JUST
DON'T UNDERSTAND.

1836
00:58:50,899 --> 00:58:51,833
WHO?

1837
00:58:51,833 --> 00:58:52,567
CASSANDRA.

1838
00:58:52,567 --> 00:58:55,470
YOU CAN TELL THAT GIRL
AIN'T STRUGGLED AT ALL.

1839
00:58:55,470 --> 00:58:57,305
DO YOU KNOW WHAT
I MEAN?

1840
00:58:57,305 --> 00:58:58,540
IT'S LIKE SHE'S
ALMOST LIKE A MACHINE.

1841
00:58:58,540 --> 00:58:59,908
DOES SHE RECHARGE
HER BATTERY?

1842
00:58:59,908 --> 00:59:00,909
WHERE DOES
SHE PLUG IN?

1843
00:59:00,909 --> 00:59:03,445
IT'S LIKE, "I'M BREAKING
DOWN RIGHT NOW."

1844
00:59:03,445 --> 00:59:05,380
(laughing)

1845
00:59:05,380 --> 00:59:07,148
CASSANDRA
IS A WEIRDO.

1846
00:59:07,148 --> 00:59:09,384
SHE JUST THINKS SHE'S ALL
MISS PRIMPER AND PROPER

1847
00:59:09,384 --> 00:59:10,719
'CAUSE SHE'S
PAGEANT QUEEN.

1848
00:59:10,719 --> 00:59:12,287
GIRL, I WAS JUST
TALKING ABOUT YOU.

1849
00:59:12,287 --> 00:59:13,221
WHAT DID I DO?

1850
00:59:13,221 --> 00:59:14,556
YOU DIDN'T DO
ANYTHING, DUDE.

1851
00:59:14,556 --> 00:59:15,190
WE'RE WAITING
FOR YOU--

1852
00:59:15,190 --> 00:59:17,058
LIKE WE ALMOST FEEL
LIKE YOU'RE A ROBOT.

1853
00:59:17,058 --> 00:59:18,426
YOU'RE JUST THE PAGEANT
GIRL AND IT'S--

1854
00:59:18,426 --> 00:59:19,561
LIKE,
WHAT'S THE DEAL?

1855
00:59:19,561 --> 00:59:21,563
YOU KNOW HOW SOCIOPATHS
DON'T FEEL EMOTION

1856
00:59:21,563 --> 00:59:22,731
AND THAT'S WHY
THEY CAN KILL PEOPLE

1857
00:59:22,731 --> 00:59:23,732
WITHOUT EVER, LIKE,

1858
00:59:23,732 --> 00:59:25,200
FEELING BAD
ABOUT IT?

1859
00:59:25,200 --> 00:59:26,701
ONLY I NEVER
KILLED ANYBODY.

1860
00:59:26,701 --> 00:59:28,603
(crickets chirping)

1861
00:59:28,603 --> 00:59:30,338
THIS IS SO BIZARRE.

1862
00:59:30,338 --> 00:59:31,640
I'M LIKE,
WHAT IS UNDERNEATH

1863
00:59:31,640 --> 00:59:32,374
THOSE EYEBALLS?

1864
00:59:32,374 --> 00:59:33,541
WHAT IS SHE THINKING?

1865
00:59:33,541 --> 00:59:35,176
IT'S NOT THAT I DON'T
FEEL COMFORTABLE

1866
00:59:35,176 --> 00:59:37,145
SHARING THINGS
WITH OTHER PEOPLE.

1867
00:59:37,145 --> 00:59:39,247
IT'S JUST THAT I'M
NOT AN EMOTIONAL PERSON.

1868
00:59:39,247 --> 00:59:41,716
TYRA MAIL!

1869
00:59:41,716 --> 00:59:43,752
TYRA MAIL!

1870
00:59:43,752 --> 00:59:45,620
TYRA MAIL!

1871
00:59:45,620 --> 00:59:46,821
SO HERE IT IS, GUYS.

1872
00:59:46,821 --> 00:59:48,390
"IT'S A BIRD,
IT'S A PLANE.

1873
00:59:48,390 --> 00:59:50,158
NO, IT'S A TOP
MODEL IN THE MAKING.

1874
00:59:50,158 --> 00:59:52,193
BE READY AT 5:30 A.M."

1875
00:59:52,193 --> 00:59:55,430
(squealing)

1876
00:59:55,430 --> 00:59:58,533
♪♪♪

1877
01:00:07,008 --> 01:00:07,575
ALL RIGHT.

1878
01:00:07,575 --> 01:00:08,743
GOOD MORNING,
HOW ARE YOU?

1879
01:00:08,743 --> 01:00:10,078
I KNOW IT'S EARLY.

1880
01:00:10,078 --> 01:00:12,847
SO TODAY,
WE ARE GOING TO HAVE

1881
01:00:12,847 --> 01:00:16,951
YOU GIRLS FLYING
AS SUPERHEROES.

1882
01:00:16,951 --> 01:00:18,853
YEAH!

1883
